  "//": "getGpsTrack, getActivityRecord, getActivityIntervals and getActivityStreams are read outside the screen reads on purpose: a track and a stored body are large and belong on the path that needs them, not on every mount. The engine's doc comment on activity_detail_data carries the measurement. setInteracting is a command: a touch signal pushed from the root view that the engine uses to pace its background passes, and no screen read carries it. RouteManager.liveOverlaps measures a polyline the recording screen holds in memory against saved route groups; the polyline is an argument, so it is a computation and not data a screen read could return.",
